Description: BITLK: skip unknown metadata entries inside usable VMKs
 Recent Windows 11 builds add a small entry (value 0x24) to the clear-key VMK
 of suspended / not-yet-activated device-encryption volumes. libcryptsetup
 rejected the whole device ("Unexpected metadata entry value '36' found when
 parsing supported Volume Master Key"), so udisks/GNOME Files could not unlock
 the Windows partition. Unknown entries are now logged and skipped, as they
 already are for unsupported VMKs; the keys actually needed are still checked
 when the volume is opened.
Author: sb4edge-linux
--- a/lib/bitlk/bitlk.c
+++ b/lib/bitlk/bitlk.c
@@ -372,12 +372,7 @@
 		} else if (key_entry_value == BITLK_ENTRY_VALUE_TPM_KEY && (*vmk)->protection == BITLK_PROTECTION_TPM) {
 			;
 		} else {
-			if (supported) {
-				log_err(cd, _("Unexpected metadata entry value '%u' found when parsing supported Volume Master Key."), key_entry_value);
-				return -EINVAL;
-			} else {
-				log_dbg(cd, "Unexpected metadata entry value '%u' found when parsing unsupported VMK.", key_entry_value);
-			}
+			log_dbg(cd, "Skipping unknown metadata entry value '%u' in %s VMK.", key_entry_value, supported ? "supported" : "unsupported");
 		}
 
 		start += key_entry_size;
